{"query":"how to undo last git commit","results":[{"position":1,"site_name":"www.git-tower.com","snippet":"In case you're using the Tower Git client, you can simply hit CMD+Z (or CTRL+Z on Windows) to undo the last commit: You can use this familiar keyboard shortcut ...","title":"How to Undo a Commit in Git (Reset, Revert, or Rebase)","url":"https://www.git-tower.com/learn/git/faq/undo-last-commit"},{"date":"17 years ago","position":2,"site_name":"stackoverflow.com","snippet":"I accidentally committed the wrong files to Git but haven't pushed the commit to the server yet. How do I undo those commits from the local repository?","title":"How do I undo the most recent local commits in Git?","url":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/927358/how-do-i-undo-the-most-recent-local-commits-in-git"},{"date":"Jan 6, 2026","position":3,"site_name":"github.com","snippet":"You can use git reset with the --soft or --mixed option to undo the last commit while keeping your changes. Steps: Undo the last commit but keep changes staged:.","title":"undo the last commit · community · Discussion #183621","url":"https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/183621"},{"date":"Nov 29, 2025","position":4,"site_name":"gitprotect.io","snippet":"Fortunately, there is a safe solution – the git revert command operation. With it, we can undo changes from a specific commit. We don't have to ...","title":"How to Undo a Commit in Git - Blog","url":"https://gitprotect.io/blog/how-to-undo-a-commit-in-git/"},{"position":5,"site_name":"git-scm.com","snippet":"Undoing things with git restore ... Git version 2.23.0 introduced a new command: git restore . It's basically an alternative to git reset which we just covered.","title":"Undoing Things","url":"https://git-scm.com/book/en/v2/Git-Basics-Undoing-Things"},{"date":"Aug 31, 2021","position":6,"site_name":"www.freecodecamp.org","snippet":"You can find the name of the commit you want to revert using [git log](https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/git-log-command/) . The first commit ...","title":"Git Revert Commit – How to Undo the Last Commit","url":"https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/git-revert-commit-how-to-undo-the-last-commit/"},{"date":"2 years ago","position":7,"site_name":"www.reddit.com","snippet":"And then they'll have to git fetch && git checkout main && git reset --hard origin/main . This will force-reset their local main branch to the ...","title":"How to undo pushed commits : r/git","url":"https://www.reddit.com/r/git/comments/1adye9m/how_to_undo_pushed_commits/"},{"date":"Nov 30, 2023","position":8,"site_name":"www.warp.dev","snippet":"Explore ways to undo a commit, including git reset, git checkout, and git revert with git while preserving commit history.","title":"How To Undo Your Last Git Commit(s) - Warp","url":"https://www.warp.dev/terminus/git-undo-commit"},{"date":"Nov 30, 2024","position":9,"site_name":"blog.openreplay.com","snippet":"Identify the commit you want to revert using git log . Use git revert <commit-hash> to create a new commit that undoes the specified commit.","title":"Undoing Git Commits After Push: Safely Revert Changes ...","url":"https://blog.openreplay.com/git-undo-commit/"},{"date":"Jul 8, 2022","position":10,"site_name":"www.akamai.com","snippet":"To undo the changes, perform a hard reset using the --hard option. Specify HEAD~1 to revert to the commit preceding the current commit. If the ...","title":"Undo a Git Commit: A Step-by-Step Guide | Linode Docs","url":"https://www.akamai.com/docs/guides/how-to-undo-git-commit/"}],"total_results":10,"page":0}
